{"toolCallId":"call_5b3da737f5f44d95a1da4f9e78ca6544","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports an Overall Completion percentage but always exits 0, so a caller cannot fail a build on an incomplete spec folder. This adds a --min-percent <N> gate that exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N and 0 otherwise, leaving the printed report untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints an Overall Completion percentage and then exits 0 on every run, including a run whose folder is nearly empty. A caller that wants to fail a build on an incomplete spec folder has to parse the printed report or the JSON field itself, and each caller that does so re-implements the comparison.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd a `--min-percent <N>` option so one invocation both reports and gates: exit 3 when the reported Overall Completion is below N, exit 0 otherwise, with the report unchanged.\n\n### Measured Behavior\n\n```text\n$ mkdir -p /tmp/minpct-demo && printf '%s\\n' '# Demo spec' '' '## 1. METADATA' 'Level 1' '' '## 2. PROBLEM' '[PLACEHOLDER]' '## 3. SCOPE' '[PLACEHOLDER]' '' '## 4. REQUIREMENTS' '[PLACEHOLDER]' '## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA' 'None' '## 6. RISKS' 'None' > /tmp/minpct-demo/spec.md\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh /tmp/minpct-demo; echo \"EXIT=$?\"\nSpec Folder: /tmp/minpct-demo\nFiles Analyzed: 1\nOverall Completion: 77%\nTotal Placeholders: 3\nTotal Content Lines: 13\nStatus: ✅ Good - Well underway\nEXIT=0\n```\n\nThe fixture reports `Overall Completion: 77%` and still exits `0`, so section 2's claim that no run gates on the percentage is measured rather than recalled. `77` is the number every requirement below uses as its below-threshold case.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add a `--min-percent <N>` option to the argument parser in `calculate-completeness.sh`.\n- Exit 3 after printing the report when Overall Completion is below N, and exit 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Reject a missing, empty or non-integer N with exit 1 and an error on stderr.\n- Document the option in `show_help`.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing the completion formula or the placeholder patterns - the percentage stays the number the script already reports.\n- Changing the text or JSON report - the option adds an exit status only.\n- Gating `--file` single-file mode - a single file has no Overall Completion to compare, so the combination is rejected rather than guessed.\n- Adding a default threshold or reading one from configuration - the option is opt-in per invocation.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh | Modify | Parse `--min-percent <N>`, validate it, document it in `show_help`, and exit 3 below the threshold |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | With `--min-percent <N>`, a spec-folder run whose Overall Completion is below N exits 3 | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 3 on the 77% fixture |\n| REQ-002 | With `--min-percent <N>`, a spec-folder run whose Overall Completion is at or above N exits 0 | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 70 /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 0, and `--min-percent 77` also exits 0 |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-003 | The printed report is byte-identical with and without `--min-percent` | `diff` of the two runs prints nothing for both the text and the `--json` report |\n| REQ-004 | `--help` documents the option and its exit status | `calculate-completeness.sh --help \\| rg -c -- '--min-percent'` prints 2 |\n| REQ-005 | A missing, empty or non-integer N exits 1 with an error on stderr | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 1, and `--min-percent abc /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 1 |\n| REQ-006 | `--min-percent` combined with `--file` exits 1, because no Overall Completion exists to compare | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 --file specs/x/spec.md` exits 1 with an error naming the conflict |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` prints `Overall Completion: 77%` and exits 3.\n- **SC-002**: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 70 /tmp/minpct-demo` prints the same report and exits 0.\n- **SC-003**: `diff <(calculate-completeness.sh /tmp/minpct-demo) <(calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo)` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required for the percentage math | No percentage, so no comparison | The existing `command -v bc` guard runs before the gate and exits 1 |\n| Risk | Exit 3 is the spec-script taxonomy's system-error code, so a caller may read a below-threshold result as a crash | A caller retries or aborts on what is a normal gate result | Document exit 3 in `show_help` and in the script's trailing exit-code comment, and name it in REQ-004 |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns an arithmetic comparison of a non-integer N into a bare bash abort instead of the intended error | Unclear exit status and no message | Validate N against `^[0-9]+$` before any comparison, and test both `abc` and a missing value |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does a threshold of exactly N count as passing? Decision: yes, `--min-percent 77` exits 0 on a 77% folder, because the requirement reads \"below N\".\n- Should the gate apply to `--file` mode? Decision: no. A single file reports a per-file `Completion` rather than an Overall Completion, so the combination exits 1 instead of silently comparing a different number.\n- Should N above 100 be rejected? Decision: no. It always exits 3, which is the honest answer for a threshold no folder can reach, and rejecting it would add a rule the feature did not ask for.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"calculate-completeness.sh reports an Overall Completion percentage but always exits 0, so a caller cannot fail a build on an incomplete spec folder. This adds a --min-percent <N> gate that exits 3 when the reported percentage is below N and 0 otherwise, leaving the printed report untouched.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints an Overall Completion percentage and then exits 0 on every run, including a run whose folder is nearly empty. A caller that wants to fail a build on an incomplete spec folder has to parse the printed report or the JSON field itself, and each caller that does so re-implements the comparison.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd a `--min-percent <N>` option so one invocation both reports and gates: exit 3 when the reported Overall Completion is below N, exit 0 otherwise, with the report unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n\n```text\n$ mkdir -p /tmp/minpct-demo && printf '%s\\n' '# Demo spec' '' '## 1. METADATA' 'Level 1' '' '## 2. PROBLEM' '[PLACEHOLDER]' '## 3. SCOPE' '[PLACEHOLDER]' '' '## 4. REQUIREMENTS' '[PLACEHOLDER]' '## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA' 'None' '## 6. RISKS' 'None' > /tmp/minpct-demo/spec.md\n$ bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh /tmp/minpct-demo; echo \"EXIT=$?\"\nSpec Folder: /tmp/minpct-demo\nFiles Analyzed: 1\nOverall Completion: 77%\nTotal Placeholders: 3\nTotal Content Lines: 13\nStatus: ✅ Good - Well underway\nEXIT=0\n```\n\nThe fixture reports `Overall Completion: 77%` and still exits `0`, so section 2's claim that no run gates on the percentage is measured rather than recalled. `77` is the number every requirement below uses as its below-threshold case.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add a `--min-percent <N>` option to the argument parser in `calculate-completeness.sh`.\n- Exit 3 after printing the report when Overall Completion is below N, and exit 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Reject a missing, empty or non-integer N with exit 1 and an error on stderr.\n- Document the option in `show_help`.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing the completion formula or the placeholder patterns - the percentage stays the number the script already reports.\n- Changing the text or JSON report - the option adds an exit status only.\n- Gating `--file` single-file mode - a single file has no Overall Completion to compare, so the combination is rejected rather than guessed.\n- Adding a default threshold or reading one from configuration - the option is opt-in per invocation.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh | Modify | Parse `--min-percent <N>`, validate it, document it in `show_help`, and exit 3 below the threshold |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | With `--min-percent <N>`, a spec-folder run whose Overall Completion is below N exits 3 | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 3 on the 77% fixture |\n| REQ-002 | With `--min-percent <N>`, a spec-folder run whose Overall Completion is at or above N exits 0 | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 70 /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 0, and `--min-percent 77` also exits 0 |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-003 | The printed report is byte-identical with and without `--min-percent` | `diff` of the two runs prints nothing for both the text and the `--json` report |\n| REQ-004 | `--help` documents the option and its exit status | `calculate-completeness.sh --help \\| rg -c -- '--min-percent'` prints 2 |\n| REQ-005 | A missing, empty or non-integer N exits 1 with an error on stderr | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 1, and `--min-percent abc /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 1 |\n| REQ-006 | `--min-percent` combined with `--file` exits 1, because no Overall Completion exists to compare | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 --file specs/x/spec.md` exits 1 with an error naming the conflict |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` prints `Overall Completion: 77%` and exits 3.\n- **SC-002**: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 70 /tmp/minpct-demo` prints the same report and exits 0.\n- **SC-003**: `diff <(calculate-completeness.sh /tmp/minpct-demo) <(calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo)` prints nothing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc`, already required for the percentage math | No percentage, so no comparison | The existing `command -v bc` guard runs before the gate and exits 1 |\n| Risk | Exit 3 is the spec-script taxonomy's system-error code, so a caller may read a below-threshold result as a crash | A caller retries or aborts on what is a normal gate result | Document exit 3 in `show_help` and in the script's trailing exit-code comment, and name it in REQ-004 |\n| Risk | `set -euo pipefail` turns an arithmetic comparison of a non-integer N into a bare bash abort instead of the intended error | Unclear exit status and no message | Validate N against `^[0-9]+$` before any comparison, and test both `abc` and a missing value |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does a threshold of exactly N count as passing? Decision: yes, `--min-percent 77` exits 0 on a 77% folder, because the requirement reads \"below N\".\n- Should the gate apply to `--file` mode? Decision: no. A single file reports a per-file `Completion` rather than an Overall Completion, so the combination exits 1 instead of silently comparing a different number.\n- Should N above 100 be rejected? Decision: no. It always exits 3, which is the honest answer for a threshold no folder can reach, and rejecting it would add a rule the feature did not ask for.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":2,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_6ba8d7387e9a44d9b96f19c760cf410c","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one flag to an existing bash script: parse --min-percent <N>, validate it as a non-negative integer, and turn the already-computed Overall Completion into an exit status after the report prints. The report itself stays byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Direct invocation against a fixture folder, checking output and exit status |\n\n### Overview\nAdd a `MIN_PERCENT` global and one `--min-percent` case to the existing argument loop, then compare `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` against it after `output_text`/`output_json` returns and before the final `exit 0`. Because the comparison runs last, the report prints exactly as it does today and only the process exit status changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` prints `Overall Completion: 77%` and exits 3; the same run with `--min-percent 70` exits 0\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle script branch\n\n### Key Components\n- **`calculate-completeness.sh` argument loop**: gains a `--min-percent|-m` case that stores the raw value and validates it before any analysis runs.\n- **`calculate_spec_completeness`**: unchanged; it already sets `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE`, which is the number the gate reads.\n- **Main tail after `output_text`/`output_json`**: the one new decision point, comparing `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` with `MIN_PERCENT` and choosing exit 3 or exit 0.\n\n### Data Flow\nThe argument loop sets `MIN_PERCENT` and rejects a bad value with exit 1. Analysis sets `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` exactly as it does now. The output function prints the report. Control then reaches the tail, which exits 3 when `MIN_PERCENT` is set and `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` is below it, and exits 0 in every other case.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state. Setup builds the 77% fixture and confirms today's exit 0. Implementation adds the flag, its validation, the tail gate and the help text. Verification proves the two exit statuses, the unchanged report and the rejected combinations.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nRun the script twice against the 77% fixture: `--min-percent 90` must exit 3 and `--min-percent 70` must exit 0, both printing `Overall Completion: 77%`. Then diff the plain run against the gated run for both the text and `--json` reports; both diffs must print nothing. Finally check the rejected inputs, where `--min-percent` with no value, with `abc`, and with `--file` must each exit 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n`bash` 3.2 or later and `bc`, both already required by the script. No new package, no new file and no change to any other script.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: a gated run exits 3 or 0 on the wrong side of its threshold, or the report differs from the plain run. Revert the single scoped commit to `calculate-completeness.sh`; the option disappears and every caller keeps today's always-exit-0 behavior.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one flag to an existing bash script: parse --min-percent <N>, validate it as a non-negative integer, and turn the already-computed Overall Completion into an exit status after the report prints. The report itself stays byte-identical.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2+ compatible shell script |\n| **Framework** | None |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Direct invocation against a fixture folder, checking output and exit status |\n\n### Overview\nAdd a `MIN_PERCENT` global and one `--min-percent` case to the existing argument loop, then compare `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` against it after `output_text`/`output_json` returns and before the final `exit 0`. Because the comparison runs last, the report prints exactly as it does today and only the process exit status changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` prints `Overall Completion: 77%` and exits 3; the same run with `--min-percent 70` exits 0\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle script branch\n\n### Key Components\n- **`calculate-completeness.sh` argument loop**: gains a `--min-percent` case that stores the raw value and validates it before any analysis runs.\n- **`calculate_spec_completeness`**: unchanged; it already sets `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE`, which is the number the gate reads.\n- **Main tail after `output_text`/`output_json`**: the one new decision point, comparing `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` with `MIN_PERCENT` and choosing exit 3 or exit 0.\n\n### Data Flow\nThe argument loop sets `MIN_PERCENT` and rejects a bad value with exit 1. Analysis sets `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` exactly as it does now. The output function prints the report. Control then reaches the tail, which exits 3 when `MIN_PERCENT` is set and `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` is below it, and exits 0 in every other case.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state. Setup builds the 77% fixture and confirms today's exit 0. Implementation adds the flag, its validation, the tail gate and the help text. Verification proves the two exit statuses, the unchanged report and the rejected combinations.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nRun the script twice against the 77% fixture: `--min-percent 90` must exit 3 and `--min-percent 70` must exit 0, both printing `Overall Completion: 77%`. Then diff the plain run against the gated run for both the text and `--json` reports; both diffs must print nothing. Finally check the rejected inputs, where `--min-percent` with no value, with `abc`, and with `--file` must each exit 1.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n`bash` 3.2 or later and `bc`, both already required by the script. No new package, no new file and no change to any other script.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: a gated run exits 3 or 0 on the wrong side of its threshold, or the report differs from the plain run. Revert the single scoped commit to `calculate-completeness.sh`; the option disappears and every caller keeps today's always-exit-0 behavior.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":1}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
